WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:09.000
Recently, leftists won landslide
elections in Argentina, and

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:13.290
left-of-centre candidates won key mayoral
posts in Colombia. For all its faults,

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:17.970
democracy works in Latin America. But
fair elections weren't good enough for

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:21.779
Bolivia's leftist President Evo Morales,
who was caught trying to steal an

00:00:21.779 --> 00:00:25.800
illegal fourth term, and had to flee the
country when the army sided with

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:29.880
pro-democracy protesters. In Ecuador and
Chile, leftists have tried to oust

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:35.219
democratically-elected leaders using mob
violence. The rampage continues in Chile,

00:00:35.219 --> 00:00:39.690
despite the president's decision to
reverse unpopular transit fare hikes and

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:45.300
to increase social spending. It's clear
that Latin America's leftists want power

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:49.020
by any means necessary. In Bolivia and
Ecuador,

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:53.440
authorities suspect Cuban subversion. The
narco-regime in Venezuela and the

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:58.960
narco-dictatorship in Cuba have the motive and
the means to attack the rule of law,

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:03.899
democracy, and free market policies, and
that's exactly what they'll do as long

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:07.840
as democratic governments let them act
with impunity.

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:13.860
Will Latin American democracies confront mob violence? Let us know in our poll. And let us know what

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:18.030
other topics you'd like our scholars to
cover in 60 seconds, and be sure to like

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:23.659
and subscribe for more research and
videos from AEI.

